<title>TURKEY: Turk cb reserve at record high at $17.3 billion.</title>
<headline>Turk cb reserve at record high at $17.3 billion.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves rose by $1.32 billion to a record high of $17.263 billion in the week to September 27.</p>
<p>Bankers said the government's sale of foreign currency denominated bonds of $1.12 billion accounted for the sharp rise in the central bank reserve.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>		   Sept 27	Sept 20	end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve  17.263	 15.943	  12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve    1.383	  1.383	   1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve  18.646	 17.326	  13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, fell by $192 million to $27.656 billion in the week ending September 13, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
